    "selected": "none (baseline)",
    "rationale": "The positive class is 19.5% \u2014 imbalanced but not extreme, so the question is which correction actually helps rather than whether to apply one. Strategies were compared on identical held-out validation patients. SMOTE is included for completeness but is a poor fit for this feature space: interpolating between ordinal-coded categoricals synthesises organism and antibiotic codes that correspond to no real entity, and interpolating sparse prior-exposure counts invents patient histories. Random undersampling discards a large share of the majority class and with it the informative lab and history patterns that only appear in susceptible isolates."
  },
